cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sindhinorm or the MorphoTok-SD-UR materials, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "sindhinorm: a corpus-guided, native-validated spelling normalizer for Sindhi"
abstract: >-
  sindhinorm normalizes Sindhi text typed on mixed Urdu, Persian and Arabic keyboards.
  It decides per word, using word frequencies from Sindhi Wikipedia, and never merges
  spelling pairs that a native Sindhi speaker judged to be different words. It is part of
  MorphoTok-SD-UR, a preregistered study of morphology-aware tokenization for Sindhi and Urdu.
  Code is MIT-licensed; the bundled word list is CC BY-SA 4.0 (derived from Sindhi Wikipedia).
authors:
  - family-names: Kaleem
    given-names: Arsalan
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArsalanKaleem/MorphoTok-SD-UR"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/sindhinorm/"
keywords:
  - Sindhi
  - text normalization
  - Arabic script
  - Unicode
  - spelling variation
  - low-resource NLP
